{"symbol":"PTG.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:55:55Z","info":{"address1":"ul. Botaniczna 20","city":"Gdansk","zip":"80-298","country":"Poland","phone":"48 512 532 401","website":"https://poltreg.bio","industry":"Biotechnology","industryKey":"biotechnology","industryDisp":"Biotechnology","sector":"Healthcare","sectorKey":"healthcare","sectorDisp":"Healthcare","longBusinessSummary":"Poltreg S.A., a biotechnology company, researches and develops therapies for autoimmune diseases in Poland. Its product pipeline includes PTG-OO7 + Rituximab which is in phase II clinical trial to treat presymptomatic T1D; MOG CAR-Treg which is in phase I clinical trial for the treatment of multiple sclerosis, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; Multi-Edit/Allo MOG CAR-Treg which is in preclinical trial to treat multiple sclerosis, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; and Antigen-specific T-regulatory cell (Tregs) which is in preclinical trial to treat T1D. The company also develops CD6/CTLA4 CAR-Treg which is in phase I clinical trial to treat stage 3 T1D; CD6/CTLA4 CAR-Treg which is in preclinical trial for the treatment of vitiligo, atopic derm, psoriasis, and alopecia areata; CD6/CTLA4 CAR-Treg which is in preclinical trial to treat multiple sclerosis, amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis; and PTG-OO7 + Rituximab which is in preclinical trial to treat presympt T1D. In addition, it is developing cell therapies involve the use of human cells to regenerate a patient's damaged tissues or organs. The company was founded in 2015 and is headquartered in Gdansk, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":34,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Piotr  Trzonkowsk","title":"President of the Management Board","fiscalYear":2024,"totalPay":640000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Paulina  Kocenko-Merks","title":"CFO & Member of Management Board","fiscalYear":2024,"totalPay":375